    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Greens Fork takes its name from the Greens Fork River that runs through the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greens_Fork%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office has been in operation since 1828, making it one of the oldest continuously running services in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greens_Fork%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Greens Fork’s growth in the mid‑19th century was spurred by fertile farmlands and the arrival of the railroad, which opened new markets for local farmers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://allthingsusa.blog/greens-fork-indiana-uncover-hidden-gems-timeless-charm",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Old Millstone Mercantile, a historic general store, still serves as a community hub and local café, welcoming visitors from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. on weekdays and Saturdays.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://allthingsusa.blog/greens-fork-indiana-uncover-hidden-gems-timeless-charm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2002, Greens Fork built a central wastewater treatment plant, a sanitary sewer system, and a lift station to pump sewage to the treatment facility.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greens_Fork%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Greens Fork Community Church, an architectural landmark, hosts services on Sundays and offers tours by appointment, reflecting the town’s enduring religious heritage.",
